
      <html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
      <head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>THEXRA Solution Brief</title></head>
      <body>
        <h1>THEXRA ENTERPRISE SOLUTION BRIEF</h1>
        <h2>1. Client Problem Statement</h2><p>Metro Urban Development Authority faces significant communication friction in Government public zoning reviews because physical foam scale models and static 2D PDF blueprints fail to convey spatial proportions, shadow analysis, and civil infrastructure impacts to non-technical stakeholders, resulting in protracted deliberations and repeated revision requests.</p>
        <h2>2. Proposed Solution</h2><p>THEXRA View replaces physical foam scale models and static 2D PDF blueprints with a large-format multi-touch interactive review console, enabling city council members and the public to dynamically explore 3D infrastructure layouts, simulate environmental impacts, and evaluate zoning variances collaboratively.</p>
        <h2>3. Technology Selection</h2><p>Interactive Display — THEXRA View (Government Edition)</p>
      </body>
      </html>
    